You are implementing Task 2: Parallelize action loading loop

## Task Description

The `for...of` loop in `getExternalUserActionData.ts` calls `getExtActionData()` sequentially for every action and its template — the most expensive part. With 8 actions, each needing 2 reads (doc + languages subcollection) plus 2 more for the template, this is ~32 sequential Firestore round-trips.

**Files:**
- Modify: `functions/checkpoint-api/src/features/externalUserActions/getExternalUserActionData.ts`

**Step 1: Replace the for loop with Promise.all**

Find the `for (const action of extActionsSnap.docs)` loop (currently around line 146) and replace it with:

```ts
actionsDataList = await Promise.all(
  extActionsSnap.docs.map(async (action) => {
    const id = action.id;
    const data = action.data();

    const [feedbackActionData, templateActionData] = await Promise.all([
      getExtActionData(
        `Buildings/${queryParams.buildingId}/externalFeedbackActions/${id}`
      ),
      data.template
        ? getExtActionData(data.template?._path?.segments?.join("/"))
        : Promise.resolve({}),
    ]);

    return { ...templateActionData, ...feedbackActionData };
  })
);

actionData = actionsDataList.find(
  (a: any) => a.id === queryParams.extActionId
);
```

Note: the original loop also set `actionData` if `id === queryParams.extActionId`. The replacement uses `.find()` after all actions are resolved.

Also: the `extActionsSnap` and `extViewsSnap` fetches (the collection-level reads) are currently sequential too. Parallelize them as well:

```ts
const [extActionsSnap, extViewsSnap] = await Promise.all([
  buildingRef.collection("externalFeedbackActions").get(),
  buildingRef.collection("externalFeedbackViews").get(),
]);

if (extActionsSnap.empty) {
  throw new NotFoundError("External feedback actions");
}
if (extViewsSnap.empty) {
  throw new NotFoundError("External feedback views");
}
```

And replace the `for (const view of extViewsSnap.docs)` loop with a simple `.map()`:

```ts
viewsDataList = extViewsSnap.docs.map((view) => ({
  id: view.id,
  ...view.data(),
}));
```

